  "title": "Dutch trading post at Dejima",
  "summary": "In 1641 the Dutch trading post was moved from Hirado to Dejima, a fan-shaped island built by reclaiming sea at Nagasaki in 1636 to house Portuguese traders. It was the headquarters of the Dutch East India Company in Japan, under close Japanese oversight, and the only place where trade with western countries was allowed.",
